# an override is about two classes. Two declarations in ONE class that answer
# to the same call are record 0012's ambiguous call and always were, and
# nothing about inheritance makes one of them win.
#
# Since 2026-09-24 the second declaration is an error on its own too: two
# functions of one name and the same parameters cannot both stand, since no
# call could ever choose between them. The call is still reported, which is
# what this case pins
class Shape:
    def pick : i32
        @a : i32
        return a

    def pick : i32
        @a : i32
        return 0

def main : i32
    @s : Shape
    return s.pick(1)
